        {
          "tool": "finish",
          "arguments": {
            "message": "The duplicate reply comes from the order playbook handing control back to the main agent after already answering.\n\nIn `conversation-fixture`, the trace shows one tool call, a playbook answer, a return to main in the same turn, and a second answer from main. The preview instructions explain why: the order playbook says to tell the visitor the result, then **always return to main**; main is instructed to answer visitor requests.\n\nThe proposed fix is to let the playbook own the answer and wait for the next visitor message, returning to main when that new request needs another capability. Alternatively, if main should own the answer, the playbook should hand back its result without answering the visitor. This follows [Voiceflow guidance](https://www.voiceflow.com/docs) on giving the final answer one owner.\n\nDiagnosis only: configuration in `project-fixture` preview is unchanged. No tests or publishing were performed."
          },
          "responseSHA256": "a7a960a481aef5e44dcccdccb6c6b33c3b70544ec6a04747a464734dfe1eaaf8"
